cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pyheat3d, please cite it as below."
title: "pyheat3d: explicit heat-equation and Jacobi stencils at the GPU memory roofline, from Python"
abstract: >-
  Explicit FTCS heat equation and Jacobi iteration (5-point 2D, 7-point 3D stencils) implemented
  across NumPy, PyTorch eager, torch.compile, Triton, NVIDIA Warp, Numba-CUDA and hand-written
  CUDA C (CuPy/NVRTC), validated against analytic solutions and benchmarked against a measured
  memory-bandwidth roofline, including temporal blocking.
type: software
authors:
